# Line endings are pinned because digests are over bytes. A verdict entry keys on
# the sha256 of every gate module, fixture and input it read, so a checkout that
# rewrote line endings (a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true: every text file
# out as CRLF) would stale every committed entry, re-run every gate on its first
# check and leave the tree dirty — for a change nobody made (SF PD-17).
# `git ls-files --eol` showed every tracked text file already i/lf when this was
# added, so nothing renormalised.
# Rejected: core.autocrlf advice in the docs (a per-machine setting the repo cannot
# enforce); `text=auto` without `eol=lf` (autocrlf=true still checks out CRLF).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Formats that can pass for text and must never be converted: an ASCII STL and a
# STEP file are plain text to git's NUL-byte heuristic, and one CR/LF rewrite
# changes the mesh digest a gate recorded. One pattern per line: gitattributes
# reads the first token as the pattern and every other token as an attribute.
*.stl -text
*.step -text
*.glb -text
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
